}{2} \\\\  & =12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533803 true] [17592186106332 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533803 true] [17592186106332 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AC \\\\  & =AM+MC \\\\  & =3+7 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=BM=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252325 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1089 "q-117335" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/3989bb27499cb1d20740ab347a1205d2c75c85c894829db054906a3bf5eb18ed.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1113 #uuid "4c8383ab-8434-5054-a648-180814c70091" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252324 1145 "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =11+5 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=CH=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{2} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252326 13194139533803 true] [17592186252325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252327 13194139533803 true] [17592186252325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252328 13194139533803 true] [17592186252325 1000 #edb/ref 1759218625232