{―}{BC}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Therefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{2} \\\\  & =17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252347 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252348 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252349 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252350 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252351 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1041 "selection" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252348 13194139533803 true] [17592186252346 1110 #uuid "5f73c6ce-729a-571b-a4f2-a88cabcb062d" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252347 1034 "16{\\text{ in}}^{2}" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533803 true] [17592186252347 1111 #uuid "048d8d61-7908-5cf0-8096-82fd4425c783" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252348 1034 "17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252348 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533803 true] [17592186252348 1111 #uuid "e6accb97-5480-52e9-931b-b2880998af09" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252349 1034 "35{\\text{ in}}^{2}" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533803 true] [17592186252349 1111 #uuid "f67e787d-757a-50dd-90e9-7c10c9a1f995" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252350 1034 "12.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533803 true] [17592186252350 1111 #uuid "2c092507-9ec5-5d2c-bcb4-98b045e089a5" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252351 1034 "7{\\text{ in}}^{2}" 13194139533803 true] [17592186252351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533803 true] [17592186252351 1111 #uuid "d5bb2628-1bb2-5b4f-a5a0-8b3db